            <title xml:id="_19" xml:lang="de">Auf das hohe Krönungs-Fest Sr. Majestät Augustus des III. Königs in Pohlen, und Churfürstens zu Sachsen wurde folgendes Drama aufgeführet</title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_dd5eaf2b">
               <persName role="composer" xml:id="_21">Johann Adolph Scheibe</persName>
               <persName role="author" xml:id="persName_b20198a1">Johann Adolph Scheibe</persName>
               <persName role="dedicatee" xml:id="_22">King Augustus III of Poland</persName>
            </contributor>
            <creation xml:id="creation_23_0">
               <date isodate="1734" xml:id="date_f97e9227">1734</date>
               <geogName xml:id="geogName_23_0">Leipzig,</geogName>
            </creation>
            <history xml:id="history_23_0">
               <eventList type="performances" xml:id="eventList_e08c2177">
                  <event xml:id="event_3f0c3281">
                     <date isodate="1734-03-03" xml:id="date_0aad636d">1734-03-03</date>
                     <geogName role="place" xml:id="geogName_74708dcf">Leipzig</geogName>
                     <biblList xml:id="biblList_216ce4fa">
                        <head xml:id="head_5b7246b2">Reviews</head>
                     </biblList>
                     <biblList xml:id="biblList_1338b6ce">
                        <head xml:id="head_d3ddf4cc">Evidence</head>
                     </biblList>
                  </event>
               </eventList>
               <p xml:id="idm121">Only the printed text to the cantata, composed for the celebration of <persName xml:id="idm122" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Augustus III</persName>’s coronation in 1734 as king of Poland, seems to have survived. The king was crowned in January for which ceremony <persName xml:id="idm123" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Johann Sebastian Bach</persName> composed the 'Drama per musica', performed by the collegium musicum in Leipzig. Shortly afterwards, Scheibe was apparently requested to compose the present cantata celebrating the coronation. Also Scheibe's was performed in Leipzig by the collegium musicum. The previous year Augustus had succeeded his father as Elector of Saxony and Bach dedicated a Mass to Augustus hoping that he would become Kapellmeister at the Saxon court. <persName xml:id="idm124" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Jan Dismas Zelenka</persName> and <persName xml:id="idm125" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Johann Adolph Hasse</persName> sought the favours of Augustus III, too, and it is possible that Scheibe’s cantata might have been composed with an eye to a possible employment at the king’s court in Dresden. There is no further information on the cantata which Scheibe wrote while in Leipzig.</p>
            </history>
